  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything yet. Renaming these fields would break two other teams' consumers of `OrderPlaced`, and I can't fix their code from here because those repos are read-only.\n\n- **billing-service** (`src/core/orderPlacedEvent.ts:38-40`, `src/core/invoice.ts:34`): its validator reads `event.totalCents`. After the rename it would reject every `OrderPlaced` event as invalid, so no invoices would be created.\n- **analytics-ingest** (`src/core/events.ts:33`): it requires `placedAt` through `reader.isoInstant(\"placedAt\")`. A missing field raises `ContractViolationError`, so ingestion would fail.\n- **web-storefront** also uses these names, but it appears to read the HTTP responses rather than the event. I'd still check it.\n\nThe rename inside orders-service itself is small. It touches the event type and builder in `src/core/events.ts` and the tests that assert on the event. The HTTP response (`responses.ts`) and the domain `Order` would keep their current names. I'd only change the event, since your request was about the event.\n\nHow do you want to handle the consumers?\n\n1. **Dual-publish transition (my recommendation).** The event carries both the old and new field names. Billing and analytics migrate on their own schedule, and we drop `totalCents` and `placedAt` afterwards.\n2. **Straight rename.** I do it now, and you coordinate with Billing and Analytics to deploy their changes first or at the same time.\n3. **Versioned event.** We publish a new event version alongside the old one.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll implement it.",
